        "<strong>Sharatz (<em>שָׁרַץ</em>) — “swarmed.”</strong> The same verb appears in Genesis 1:20–21 of fish and creeping things multiplying. Its application to humans here is unusual and faintly unsettling: Israel’s growth is described in the language of a teeming animal population, foreshadowing why the Egyptians will fear them. The cluster of five fertility verbs in this verse (<em>were fruitful, increased, multiplied, grew strong, filled</em>) deliberately echoes the creation blessing of Genesis 1:28.",
