        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (365).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Hymns on the Nativity</em> <small>(c. 365 AD)</small><p>The bush that burns yet is not consumed is, for Ephrem, the first canonical type of the Theotokos: the holy fire of divinity dwelling within the bush of Mary&#x27;s flesh without consuming it. Tewahedo iconography seats the burning bush among its earliest Marian types, and the bush is a regular figure in Marian hymnody: &#x27;the bush that bore the fire and was not burned.&#x27;</p></aside>',
        "Ephrem the Syrian, Hymns on the Nativity I.18; cp. Hymns on the Crucifixion I.2-3 (NPNF S2 V13, Gwynn/Schaff trans., Oxford 1898). PD.",
