        "holy ground",
        "comm-contextual",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Removing sandals.</strong> Footwear removal as a sign of stepping onto sacred space is well-attested across the ancient Near East and survives in Islamic and many Eastern Christian practice today. Joshua receives the same instruction at Jericho (Josh 5:15). The leather of the sandal — once an animal — is what is excluded, perhaps marking the boundary between mortal flesh and divine ground.",
