        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (365).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Hymns on the Crucifixion</em> <small>(c. 365 AD)</small><p>Aaron&#x27;s rod swallowing the rods-turned-serpents of the magicians is, for Ephrem, an early figure of the Crucified Christ swallowing the dragon: the wood that becomes a serpent becomes a devouring serpent, and the devouring is itself the salvation. The Cross — wood that becomes the throne of the Serpent-conqueror — accomplishes in reality what the rod accomplished in type.</p></aside>',
        "Ephrem the Syrian, Hymns on the Crucifixion IV.10-12 (NPNF S2 V13). PD.",
