        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (365).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Hymns on the Crucifixion</em> <small>(c. 365 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Neither shall ye break a bone thereof&#x27; — Ephrem treats this prescription as one of the most precise prophetic anchors in the Old Testament, fulfilled verbatim at Jn 19:36 when the soldiers do not break Christ&#x27;s legs. The Lamb of God remains the unbroken lamb of Exodus. Tewahedo reads Ex 12:46 and Jn 19:36 as a single canonical disclosure of the same lamb.</p></aside>',
