        "",
        "pillar of cloud",
        "comm-contextual",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>The pillar.</strong> A single pillar — cloud by day, fire by night — accompanies Israel as far as Sinai and (by 40:36–38) settles over the tabernacle. The motif fuses two ancient Near Eastern theophany images: the storm-cloud chariot of Baal/Marduk traditions and the temple-fire of cult presence. Within Exodus, it is the visible sign that the divine name now travels with this people.",
        "User original",
