        "Witness",
        "MS.",
        "<strong>Manuscript witness.</strong> iderable number of places noted in W'hich the reading of the Septuagint makes better sense than that of the Hebrew. In not a few passages the Hebrew gives no natural meaning at all ; for instance, Ex. 14. 20 ; 1 Sam. 13. 21 ; 27. 10 (where even the Authorised Version departs from the Massoretic text) ; much of 1 Kings 6 &amp; 7 ; Job 3. 14 ; 35. 15, and many other passages indicated in the Variorum Bible.",
