        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (365).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Hymns on the Crucifixion</em> <small>(c. 365 AD)</small><p>The Lord shows Moses a tree, and the tree cast into the bitter waters of Marah makes them sweet. Ephrem reads the wood as the Cross before its time: what sweetens the waters of the world is the wood of the Cross cast into them. Tewahedo Holy-Week catechesis cites Ex 15:25 as one of its principal OT cross-typology anchors.</p></aside>',
