        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (360).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Commentary on Exodus</em> <small>(c. 360 AD)</small><p>Sinai wrapped in fire and smoke is, for Ephrem, the OT diptych of Pentecost: there the fire descends on a mountain and the people may not come near; here the fire descends on heads and tongues so that the people themselves become the mountain. Tewahedo reads Ex 19:18 and Acts 2 as the before-and-after of the divine fire — the same fire that thundered now rests on the believer without consuming.</p></aside>',
        "Ephrem the Syrian, Commentary on Exodus XIX.8 (NPNF S2 V13, Gwynn/Schaff trans., Oxford 1898). PD.",
