        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (360).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Commentary on Exodus</em> <small>(c. 360 AD)</small><p>&#x27;I am the Lord thy God, which have brought thee out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of bondage&#x27; — Ephrem reads the Pascal preface as the ground of every command that follows. The commandments are not arbitrary statutes but the rule-of-life of a delivered people; only the delivered are addressed by the Decalogue. Tewahedo catechesis preserves this priority of deliverance before commandment.</p></aside>',
        "Ephrem the Syrian, Commentary on Exodus XX.1 (NPNF S2 V13, Gwynn/Schaff trans., Oxford 1898). PD.",
