        "",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (360).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Commentary on Exodus</em> <small>(c. 360 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Remember the sabbath day, to keep it holy&#x27; — Ephrem reads Sabbath-rest as the canonical sign that creation is given a goal beyond labour: the Sabbath foreshadows the eighth-day rest of the Resurrection. Tewahedo alone among the major communions preserves both observances together — Saturday-Sabbath retained from Sinai and Sunday-Lord&#x27;s-Day added from the Resurrection — and reads Ex 20:8 as the canonical anchor of the double observance.</p></aside>',
        "Ephrem the Syrian, Commentary on Exodus XX.4 (NPNF S2 V13, Gwynn/Schaff trans., Oxford 1898). PD.",
