        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (365).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Hymns on the Crucifixion</em> <small>(c. 365 AD)</small><p>Moses takes the blood and sprinkles it on the people, saying &#x27;Behold the blood of the covenant, which the Lord hath made with you concerning all these words.&#x27; Ephrem hears in this the very formula that Christ will adopt verbatim at the Last Supper: &#x27;This is the blood of the covenant.&#x27; Tewahedo Anaphora reads Ex 24:8 and Mt 26:28 as a single covenantal sentence completed by the Cross.</p></aside>',
        "Ephrem the Syrian, Hymns on the Crucifixion VI.3-5 (NPNF S2 V13). PD.",
